# Documentation Maintenance

The `docs/` folder is the canonical human-readable reference for this project. It must stay accurate.

## When to update docs

After making any of the following changes, update the relevant `docs/` file **in the same task**. Do not leave docs stale.

| Change made | File(s) to update |
|-------------|-------------------|
| New atom or organism created | `docs/04-components.md` (add component), `docs/08-project-structure.md` (add to file tree) |
| Component modified (new props, removed fields, behavior change) | `docs/04-components.md` (update schema table + notes) |
| New package added or removed | `docs/08-project-structure.md` (stack versions table), `docs/02-getting-started.md` if it affects setup |
| Engine pipeline changed | `docs/03-how-it-works.md` |
| New schema field or validation rule | `docs/03-how-it-works.md`, `docs/04-components.md` for the affected component |
| New theme added or theme system changed | `docs/06-theming.md` |
| Security model changed (sanitizer, registry, Zod schemas) | `docs/07-security.md` |
| New environment variable | `docs/02-getting-started.md` (env vars table) |
| New Cursor rule added | `docs/08-project-structure.md` (.cursor/ section) |
| New folder or significant file added | `docs/08-project-structure.md` |
| A TODO item is resolved | `docs/TODOS.md` (remove or mark resolved) |
| A new known gap or incomplete feature is identified | `docs/TODOS.md` (add it, with severity) |

## What "updating" means

- Keep descriptions accurate — if behavior changed, update the description
- Keep schema tables accurate — if a field was added/removed/renamed, update the table
- Keep the file tree in `docs/08-project-structure.md` current
- Remove entries for things that no longer exist
- Do NOT add speculative content about future features — document what exists today

## What counts as "relevant enough to document"

Document changes that affect:
- How to run or set up the project
- How the engine renders components
- What components exist and what JSON they accept
- How security works
- How themes work
- What a developer needs to know to add something new

Do NOT document:
- Internal refactors with no visible behavior change
- Renaming a variable inside a function
- Formatting fixes
